<Window x:Class="EagleBoards.App.HelpWindow"
        Icon="/Assets/EagleBoards.ico"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        Title="Help - Eagle Board Scheduler" Width="820" Height="760" WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner">
  <FlowDocumentScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
    <FlowDocument FontFamily="Segoe UI" FontSize="14" PagePadding="28,20" ColumnWidth="10000">
      <FlowDocument.Resources>
        <Style TargetType="Paragraph">
          <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,0,8" />
        </Style>
        <Style x:Key="H" TargetType="Paragraph">
          <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="19" />
          <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
          <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,16,0,6" />
        </Style>
      </FlowDocument.Resources>

      <Paragraph FontSize="24" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,4">Eagle Board Scheduler</Paragraph>
      <Paragraph Foreground="#555">Youth and adults sign in on the check-in website. Everything else happens in this window.</Paragraph>

      <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Setting up the evening</Paragraph>
      <List MarkerStyle="Decimal">
        <ListItem><Paragraph>Start the scheduler. Choose the data folder, tonight's date, the adult history and the venue network, then press <Bold>Start</Bold>.
          The first time, Windows may ask whether to allow the scheduler on the network: allow it on <Italic>private</Italic> networks, or the check-in stations can't connect.</Paragraph></ListItem>
        <ListItem><Paragraph>Point each check-in station's browser at the address shown at the bottom of the window (for example http://192.168.1.23:8080).
          Right-click the address to copy it.</Paragraph></ListItem>
        <ListItem><Paragraph>Add rooms with <Bold>+ Room</Bold>. Each room is for Final boards or Project reviews. For several project reviews in one room, add one entry per table (200A, 200B).</Paragraph></ListItem>
      </List>

      <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Status values</Paragraph>
      <List>
        <ListItem><Paragraph><Bold>Registered</Bold>: signed in and waiting.</Paragraph></ListItem>
        <ListItem><Paragraph><Bold>Seated</Bold>: the board members are in the room with the application, references and project workbook. The youth is still outside.</Paragraph></ListItem>
        <ListItem><Paragraph><Bold>InProgress</Bold>: the youth is in the room.</Paragraph></ListItem>
        <ListItem><Paragraph><Bold>Completed</Bold>: the review is over and a result is recorded.</Paragraph></ListItem>
        <ListItem><Paragraph><Bold>Postponed</Bold>: the board won't happen tonight, usually a paperwork problem.</Paragraph></ListItem>
      </List>
      <Paragraph>In the Youth list, <Bold>#</Bold> is P for pre-registered (matched a SignUpGenius sign-up) or W for walk-in, numbered in sign-in order.
        Pre-registered youth are listed first. <Bold>Min</Bold> is minutes since the youth's status last changed: how long they've waited, or how long their board has run.</Paragraph>

      <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Running a board</Paragraph>
      <Paragraph><Bold>Paperwork.</Bold> Check each youth's paperwork as they arrive. If it isn't in order, select them and press <Bold>Postpone</Bold>.</Paragraph>
      <Paragraph><Bold>Seat.</Bold> Click a waiting youth. The scheduler proposes a board: a qualified Chair, members from other units (two for a Final board, one for a project review) and a free room of the right type.
        Change the picks with the checkboxes in the Adult Board Members list and click a different room card if you like, then press <Bold>Seat Board</Bold> and confirm the chair.
        Picks you've made are kept while you click around; <Bold>Clear picks</Bold> starts over.</Paragraph>
      <Paragraph><Bold>Start.</Bold> When the members have finished reading, fetch the youth (and their Scoutmaster or Life-to-Eagle coach to introduce them; <Bold>Locate</Bold> shows where they are) and press <Bold>Start Review</Bold>.</Paragraph>
      <Paragraph><Bold>Complete.</Bold> When the board is done, press <Bold>Complete</Bold> and record the result and any notes. The room and members are freed, and a notice shows where the youth's leaders and parents are.</Paragraph>
      <Paragraph><Bold>Reset</Bold> undoes a seating (back to Registered, room and members freed). <Bold>Change Room</Bold> moves the selected room's board to another room, or swaps two boards.</Paragraph>

      <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Who may sit on a board</Paragraph>
      <List>
        <ListItem><Paragraph>A board of review has three to six members (Guide to Advancement 8.0.0.3). Fewer is refused; four to six asks you to confirm; seven is refused. A project proposal review is not a board of review; this district runs it with two, up to six.</Paragraph></ListItem>
        <ListItem><Paragraph>The chair must be someone whose role for that board type is <Bold>Chair</Bold>, and must sit on the board. If the qualified chairs are all busy, promote someone on the <Bold>Admin Tables</Bold> (Adults tab), rather than seating a Member as chair.</Paragraph></ListItem>
        <ListItem><Paragraph>Adults from the youth's own unit get a warning naming every one of them. This council doesn't permit them; you may override down to the national rule (GTA 8.0.3.0 #2), which still needs one member from outside the unit. A board made entirely of the youth's unit is refused.</Paragraph></ListItem>
        <ListItem><Paragraph>An adult already on a board, disabled for the night, or Unavailable for that board type can't be seated.</Paragraph></ListItem>
      </List>

      <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Adults</Paragraph>
      <Paragraph>Red names are on a board; grey names have gone home. <Bold>Disable</Bold> marks the selected adult as gone home; <Bold>Enable</Bold> brings them back.
        <Bold>Show all</Bold> also lists adults who are busy, gone home, or unavailable for final boards.</Paragraph>

      <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Board timers</Paragraph>
      <Paragraph>Each room holding a board shows how long it has been in its current phase. A seated board turns red when it has been convening longer than <Italic>Convene Red</Italic> (30 minutes by default); a review in progress turns orange, then red, at the Final or Project thresholds.
        Change them in <Bold>Tools &gt; Settings</Bold>. They are prompts, not limits.</Paragraph>

      <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Admin tables and reports</Paragraph>
      <Paragraph><Bold>View &gt; Admin Tables</Bold> lists every record: tonight's youth and adults, the pre-registered youth, the cumulative adult history, and rooms. Double-click a cell to edit it. Each tab can be exported to CSV.
        <Bold>File &gt; Save Report</Bold> saves tonight's board results as a CSV file for Excel.</Paragraph>

      <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Where the data is</Paragraph>
      <Paragraph>Each event night has its own folder named by date inside the data folder, holding scouts.csv, adults.csv, rooms.csv and scouts_scheduled.csv. The adult history accumulates across every night.
        These files contain personal information about minors: keep the data folder on this computer and out of shared or cloud folders.
        The files are the same format the Java version used, so either can read the other's.</Paragraph>

      <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Pre-registration</Paragraph>
      <Paragraph>With a SignUpGenius API key (a line <Italic>SUG_KEY=...</Italic> in a file named .env in the data folder, or the SUG_KEY environment variable), the scheduler imports tonight's sign-ups at start:
        youth become pre-registrations, which is what makes them "P", and adults are added to the adult history by email.</Paragraph>
    </FlowDocument>
  </FlowDocumentScrollViewer>
</Window>
